Track 1: Unaddressed Parchment Devours the Postbox
- Story & Context: Cut live to 2-inch tape in the drafty grain depot of Winter Quarters after the wedding feast turned sour, this opening salvo captured the exact moment Lev kicked over an oil lantern as the brass section clashed with a blistering 200-BPM skank beat. The room smelled of singed wool and damp earth as Mirela blew into her neckpiece until her reed split, spitting into the talkback mic before delivering the lethargic, falsetto refrain, "You wrote our pardon on kerosene paper and dropped it down the grate."
