Track 2: Madame Orlov, Did the Wire Snap Before the Seal?
- Story & Context: Written as a crawling, down-tempo confessional inside an unheated Airstream trailer parked outside Toledo, this piece features an excruciatingly lazy bassline countered by frantic palm-muted chugs that simulate a panicked heartbeat. Lev obsessively re-read a blood-smeared telegram sent from the high-rigging accident of 1994, running his finger over the unglued wax while whispering the weary neo-soul hook, "Your ink was still wet when my center of gravity fell."
