Track 3: Poste Restante at the Menagerie Gate
- Story & Context: Legend claims the final recording was captured at dawn when the remaining wedding guests wandered into the animal tents, blending the distant snarls of caged leopards with a sprawling, rotary-phased saxophone solo that hovered over detuned thrash breakdowns. The acetate lacquer bears a permanent skip where a brass snare stand collapsed under the weight of an iron trunk, immortalizing the haunted final chant, "No forwarding name, just seven ounces of sawdust in an envelope."
